    "scope": "Original save wrapper, writer, path builder, title formatter and actual SDK atoi/todigit/strcpy/strcat/strlen versus independent guarded byte and I/O rules. Valid slots 1-15, aligned/unaligned nonoverlapping buffers, byte-masked icon argument, up to 11 attempts, create/reopen failures, reset after exhaustion, 128-byte padding, 8 KiB allocation boundaries, both device prefixes, segment aliases, ignored delete/close/write results, entire fixture buffers, call graph, global pointer, stack and saved registers. Seven explicit stubs cover file I/O, allocation and printf. Does not establish physical card I/O, allocator failure, invalid filenames, oversized icons, overlapping buffers, UI/error rendering, save persistence, complete dream-state round trips or PS1 timing."
  },
